target_type: parquet
target_path: data-private/derived/ellis/study_profile.parquet
database_label: maelstrom-analytic
target_object: study_profile
target_label: study_profile (Maelstrom harmonization study spine)
manifest_path: data-public/metadata/CACHE-manifest.md
report_path: data-private/derived/manifest-validation/validation-report.md
exclude_mode: none
notes: The canonical analysis-ready rectangle is study_profile, delivered both as a
 SQLite table in data-private/derived/maelstrom/maelstrom-analytic.sqlite and as a
 parquet mirror. The parquet mirror is the validation target because it needs no DSN
 and preserves the R types the SQLite contract cannot hold.
 .
 The dementia_frame view shares study_profile's columns exactly and therefore needs no
 separate binding.
 .
 The validator collects documented columns from every markdown table whose first header
 cell reads "Column". In CACHE-manifest.md only the study_profile sections use that
 header; the companion rectangles (study_population, study_wave, study_domain,
 screening_evidence) use "Field" so their columns are not misread as phantom entries
 against this target.
